        { "id": "d", "text": "$a^2 + b^2 = c$" }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "b",
      "explanation": "Pythagoras' theorem states $a^2 + b^2 = c^2$, where $c$ is the hypotenuse (the longest side, opposite the right angle)."
